To me, all of these arguments about limits upon wishing are sort of silly.
If you think that the game is less enjoyable when you wish for, say, a quest
artifact, then DON'T WISH FOR ONE.  This has been said before.  I think the
only possible argument one could make is that such wishes tend to upset game
balance-but this has never been my experience.  The way to limit wishes is
really to control their frequency-and this is already done sufficiently, IMHO.
	(Actually, I feel the same way about limits on poly-piling.  Although
the iron golem thing is clever, I don't think it was really necesary...)

